# Claim Module Specific Rules

## LOB-Based Validation Rules

### Car Claims (QuoteTypes::CAR->id() == 1)
- Required fields: `plate_number`, `car_make`, `car_model`, `model_year`
- Plate number validation: `/^[A-Za-z0-9\-\s]+$/`
- Model year range: 1900 to current year + 1
- Conditional validation in `validateCarFields()` method

### Health Claims (QuoteTypes::HEALTH->id() == 3)
- Required fields: `claim_request_type_id`, `service_type_id`
- Service type required when claim request type is `pending-approvals`
- Conditional validation in `validateHealthFields()` method
- Uses lookup validation against `lookups` table

### Status Transitions
- Claims start with auto-set `sub_status` = `REGISTERED` on creation
- Observer monitors `sub_status` changes for closure triggers
- Auto-closure when `sub_status` reaches predefined closure states

## Claim-Specific Method Requirements

### ClaimsController
- `searchPolicies(Request $request): JsonResponse` - CAPI integration for claim creation only
- `updateDetails(ClaimDetailsUpdateRequest $request, ClaimRequest $claim): JsonResponse` - internal system
- `updateStatus(ClaimStatusUpdateRequest $request, ClaimRequest $claim): JsonResponse` - internal system
- `optimizeMessage(ClaimSendNotificationRequest $request): JsonResponse` - AI message optimization with validation
- `sendNotification(ClaimSendNotificationRequest $request, ClaimRequest $claim): JsonResponse` - send notifications with validation
- `getClaimLeadHistory(Request $request, ClaimRequest $claim): JsonResponse` - fetch all claim status history for client-side pagination
- `getClaimSubStatusLogs(Request $request, ClaimRequest $claim): JsonResponse` - fetch all sub-status changes for client-side pagination

### ClaimsService
- `searchActivePolicies(array $criteria): array` - CAPI method for claim creation only
- `checkSubStatusForClaimClosure(ClaimRequest $claim): bool` - internal closure logic
- `markClaimAsClosed(ClaimRequest $claim): ClaimRequest` - internal closure processing
- `updateClaimSubStatusToClaimRegistered(ClaimRequest $claim): void` - internal status setting
- `getClaimLeadHistory(int $claimId): array` - optimized single-query fetch of claim_activities for parent status transitions using LAG window function for client-side pagination
- `getClaimSubStatusLogs(int $claimId): array` - optimized single-query fetch of claim_activities for sub-status transitions using LAG window function for client-side pagination

### ClaimRequest Model
- `scopeAssignedTo(Builder $query, int $userId): Builder`
- `scopeByLineOfBusiness(Builder $query, string $lob): Builder`
- `scopeOpenClaims(Builder $query): Builder`
- `canBeClosed(): bool` - business rule validation
- `assignTo(int $userId): self` - assignment with validation

### ClaimActivity Model
- `scopeForClaimRequest(Builder $query, int $claimRequestId): Builder`
- `scopeForClaimUuid(Builder $query, string $claimUuid): Builder`
- `scopeByStatus(Builder $query, int $statusId): Builder`
- `scopeCreatedBy(Builder $query, int $userId): Builder`
- `scopeWithAiComments(Builder $query): Builder`
- `scopeRecent(Builder $query, int $days): Builder`
- `hasAiComment(): bool` - check for AI-generated comments
- `getDisplayComment(): ?string` - get appropriate comment for display
- `createForClaim()` - static method for creating claim activities

## Claim-Specific Validation Rules

### Request Validation Classes
- `ClaimStoreRequest` - Initial claim creation validation
- `ClaimDetailsUpdateRequest` - Claim information updates with LOB-specific rules
- `ClaimStatusUpdateRequest` - Status transition validation
- `ClaimSendNotificationRequest` - Notification sending with AI message optimization validation

### Validation Implementation
- Car LOB check: `$quoteTypeId == QuoteTypes::CAR->id()`
- Health LOB check: `$quoteTypeId == QuoteTypes::HEALTH->id()`
- Conditional field validation using `withValidator()` method
- Uses `filled()` method to check field presence

### Validation Patterns
- Plate number: `/^[A-Za-z0-9\-\s]+$/` (actual pattern from implementation)
- Standard field trimming in `prepareForValidation()`
- Uppercase transformation for plate numbers

### Notification Validation (`ClaimSendNotificationRequest`)
- Required fields: `customer_message`, `ai_optimized_message`, `claim_sub_status_id`
- Message validation: both customer and AI optimized messages required as strings
- Sub-status validation: must exist in `claim_sub_statuses` table
- Handles AI message optimization and notification sending validation

## Observer-Specific Business Logic

### ClaimRequestObserver Requirements
- Auto-set `sub_status` to `REGISTERED` on creation
- Monitor `sub_status` changes for auto-closure triggers
- Update `is_closed` flag when status reaches closure states
- Log all status transitions with user context

### Monitored Fields for Business Rules
- `status`, `sub_status`, `assigned_to`, `line_of_business`

## CAPI Integration Requirements

### Policy Search for Claim Creation Only
- `ClaimsService::searchActivePolicies()` method for claim creation workflow
- CAPI integration only used during initial claim creation process
- Handle CAPI timeout/error scenarios gracefully during claim creation
- All other claim operations (updates, status changes, details) handled within current system

### Controller Integration
- `searchPolicies()` endpoint for AJAX policy lookup during claim creation
- JSON response format for frontend claim creation forms

## Frontend Claim-Specific Patterns

### Component Organization
- `ClaimDetails.vue` - Claim information display and editing
- `ClaimStatus.vue` - Status management component
- `ClaimDocuments.vue` - Document upload and management
- `ClaimFilters.vue` - Claims listing filters

### Permission-Based Rendering
- `claims.view`, `claims.create`, `claims.update`, `claims.delete`
- Conditional display of actions based on user permissions
- CAPI policy search only available during claim creation process

### Event Communication
- `updateClaimDetails`, `updateClaimStatus`, `documentUploaded` events
- Parent-child component communication patterns
- Policy search events only during claim creation workflow

### Vue Components Structure
- `ClaimDetails.vue` - Main claim information display and editing
- `ClaimStatus.vue` - Status management by team lead
- `ClaimSubStatusAndCustomerUpdate.vue` - Sub-status updates and customer notifications
- `ClaimDocuments.vue` - Document upload, view, and management
- `CustomerDetails.vue` - Customer information display
- `ClaimLeadHistory.vue` - AuditLogs-style DataTable showing parent status transitions with built-in pagination (15 rows per page)
- `ClaimSubStatusLogs.vue` - AuditLogs-style DataTable showing sub-status changes with built-in pagination (15 rows per page)

